  "verbalization": "Coumanolignan appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step pathway involving the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including 13-cis-Retinol and Perforamone B. These compounds are known to interact with the tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B, suggesting a potential role in modulating receptor activity or signaling. The presence of Coumanolignan as a target of the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta implies a possible mechanism by which Coumanolignan influences receptor function, possibly through the regulation of intracellular potassium levels. The integration of these pathways highlights a complex network of interactions, where Coumanolignan may act as a modulator of receptor activity via the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, potentially affecting downstream signaling pathways. This mechanism underscores the importance of the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta in mediating Coumanolignan's effects on the tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B.",
